{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [Dm]sons of [C]Kohath are named in [Dm]truth
Am[Bb]ram and [F]Izhar stand to[C]gether
[Bb]Hebron and [F]Uzziel follow [C]suit
One hundred [Bb]thirty [C]three years lived [Dm]here
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The sons of [C]Izhar are counted [Dm]clear
[Bb]Korah and [F]Nepheg and Zic[C]hri too
[Bb]Descen[F]dants serving the taber[C]nacle
Their duties [Bb]fixed for Le[C]vitical [Dm]view
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
In [Bb]David's [F]time the Izharites [C]stood
As of[Bb]ficials and [F]judges over Is[C]rael
In [Bb]charge of [F]treasuries and [C]gifts
Dedi[Bb]cated [C]for the house of [Dm]God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Korah rose [C]up against Moses [Dm]there
With [Bb]Dathan and [F]Abiram from [C]Reuben
Two [Bb]hundred and [F]fifty men op[C]posed
Challeng[Bb]ing the [C]holy Levite men
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Dm]Take cen[Bb]sers and lay [F]incense on [C]fire
P[Bb]resent it before [F]the LORD to[C]morrow
The [Bb]man he [F]chooses will be [C]holy
The [Bb]Levites [C]have gone too [Dm]far
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [Bb]earth of [F]men is fallen [C]down
{end_of_verse}
